In a study, scientists provided 3D imaging and model analysis to reveal main
causes, mechanics, and potential mitigations of the problematic [ degradation
](/wiki/Wear_and_tear "Wear and tear") of the batteries over [ charge cycles
](/wiki/Charge_cycle "Charge cycle") . They found "[p]article cracking
increases and contact loss between particles and carbon-binder domain are
observed to correlate with the cell degradation" and indicates that "the
reaction heterogeneity within the thick cathode caused by the unbalanced
electron conduction is the main cause of the battery degradation over
cycling".  [178]  [179]  [ _[ additional citation(s) needed
