An increase in solar cell temperature of approximately 1 °C causes an
efficiency decrease of about 0.45%. To prevent this, a transparent [ silica
](/wiki/Silicon_dioxide "Silicon dioxide") crystal layer can be applied to
solar panels. The silica layer acts as a [ thermal black body
](/wiki/Black_body "Black body") which emits heat as [ infrared radiation
](/wiki/Infrared "Infrared") into space, cooling the cell up to 13 °C.  [45]
Radiative cooling can thus extend the life of solar cells.  [46]  Full-system
integration of solar energy and radiative cooling is referred to as a combined
SE–RC system, which have demonstrated higher energy gain per unit area when
compared to non-integrated systems.  [47]

